WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.300
The SCP Foundation is home to plenty of anomalies
whose reputations precede them.

00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:09.960
Here at SCP Explained, we've discussed quite
a few of the most notable anomalies contained

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:14.889
by the Foundation, from the wholesome half-cats
and Tickle Monsters to the nightmarish giant

00:00:14.889 --> 00:00:20.401
reptiles and reality-warping old men . But
there are very few anomalies so popular, so

00:00:20.401 --> 00:00:26.140
famous - or infamous, depending on who you
ask - that they attract a nonstop revolving

00:00:26.140 --> 00:00:31.150
door of would-be worshippers to sew chaos
all around the Foundation.

00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:34.840
What's it like to be a creature that's always
the center of attention, whether he wants

00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:36.480
to be or not?

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:43.390
Today we're looking at the lifestyle of the
involuntarily famous, SCP-2662.

00:00:43.390 --> 00:00:47.730
We took the liberty of observing a full day
in the life of the entity known by many as

00:00:47.730 --> 00:00:53.420
Cthulhu, from his morning routine to his bedtime,
and all the little moments of unplanned chaos

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:54.660
in between.

00:00:54.660 --> 00:00:59.960
With his permission, we compiled everything
we saw into a video for your entertainment!

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:03.000
Welcome to A Day in the Life of SCP-2662.

00:01:03.000 --> 00:01:05.560
9:00 AM

00:01:05.560 --> 00:01:09.170
Time to wake up, stretch your tentacles, and
get ready for the day ahead!

00:01:09.170 --> 00:01:14.860
At a respectable, not-too-early and not-too-late
time, usually around 9 AM but sometimes a

00:01:14.860 --> 00:01:21.000
little bit later if he's had a particularly
late night, SCP-2662 climbs out of bed and

00:01:21.000 --> 00:01:24.770
uses his computer to throw on one of his favorite
podcasts.

00:01:24.770 --> 00:01:29.420
Preferred topics for listening include game
reviews and news, comedic advice podcasts,

00:01:29.420 --> 00:01:31.600
and daily news roundups.

00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:35.640
What he eats for breakfast depends on the
day, but his favorite morning meals are pancakes

00:01:35.640 --> 00:01:37.490
and huevos rancheros.

00:01:37.490 --> 00:01:41.890
No matter what he's eating, he washes it down
with a tall glass of orange juice.

00:01:41.890 --> 00:01:45.869
His nutrition needs aren't like those of a
human, but it's important to start the day

00:01:45.869 --> 00:01:48.430
with a tasty meal no matter what.

00:01:48.430 --> 00:01:51.530
It's the little things that make life worth
living.

00:01:51.530 --> 00:01:55.930
While he eats his breakfast, he reads a newspaper,
brought to him by the Foundation staff each

00:01:55.930 --> 00:01:58.250
morning according to his request.

00:01:58.250 --> 00:02:02.740
The publication varies, but no matter what,
his favorite section is Arts and Style or

00:02:02.740 --> 00:02:03.770
Human Interest.

00:02:03.770 --> 00:02:08.660
He always reads the whole thing from front
to back, though, even the obituaries and wedding

00:02:08.660 --> 00:02:09.680
announcements.

00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:13.580
He only gets one a day, after all, and he
knows it's important to appreciate things

00:02:13.580 --> 00:02:16.970
to their fullest extent and take nothing for
granted.

00:02:16.970 --> 00:02:18.100
10:00 AM.

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.720
Now it's time for SCP-2662's day to really
get going.

00:02:22.720 --> 00:02:27.690
He hops in the shower and listens to another
podcast as he warms up- literally, he likes

00:02:27.690 --> 00:02:32.080
the water to be as hot as the Foundation will
allow before they complain about the utility

00:02:32.080 --> 00:02:33.080
bill.

00:02:33.080 --> 00:02:36.510
After he dries off, he gets a hankering for
a little bit of gaming.

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:40.590
Just as he starts to settle into his gaming
chair and look through his library of video

00:02:40.590 --> 00:02:45.120
games, a member of Task Force Tau-9 knocks
on the door to his containment room.

00:02:45.120 --> 00:02:46.840
"Hey, are you busy?"

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:48.989
"Not really, something going on?"

00:02:48.989 --> 00:02:52.870
"Yeah...we're just keeping an eye on a couple
religious groups of interest.

00:02:52.870 --> 00:02:56.380
According to the chatter on the forums, and
a few of the leaders' social media accounts,

00:02:56.380 --> 00:02:58.970
they might be planning something disruptive.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:03.110
Lots of posts about a "Day of Great Freedom"
and "Unleashing the Lord of Madness Upon the

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:04.180
Pathetic World."

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.180
Cthulhu sighs.

00:03:05.180 --> 00:03:08.670
"Must be a day that ends in 'Y'."

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:09.670
"Sorry, buddy."

00:03:09.670 --> 00:03:12.010
The officer shrugs, not sure what else to
say.

00:03:12.010 --> 00:03:16.300
Clearly the two of them have spent their fair
share of days fending off mad cultists.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:21.480
"You know the drill, if anyone who's not supposed
to be here shows up, starts sacrificing goats

00:03:21.480 --> 00:03:23.340
and such, just let us know.

00:03:23.340 --> 00:03:27.200
Hopefully, it won't come to that, we should
stop them before they get that far."

00:03:27.200 --> 00:03:28.220
"Hope so.

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:32.140
Last time they got blood everywhere, and broke
my disk copy of Resident Evil 4."

00:03:32.140 --> 00:03:33.360
12:00 PM.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.540
Time flies when you're having fun, and when
you're pacing back and forth, worried about

00:03:37.540 --> 00:03:40.709
cultists breaking in to bother you with who
knows what.

00:03:40.709 --> 00:03:44.599
Before long, it's 12:00, and that means lunchtime!

00:03:44.599 --> 00:03:49.160
When it comes to lunch, SCP-2662 has simple
tastes.

00:03:49.160 --> 00:03:54.130
He likes a good old grilled cheese and tomato
soup, a bean burrito, or a steaming bowl of

00:03:54.130 --> 00:03:55.130
ramen.

00:03:55.130 --> 00:03:59.159
With that, he's partial to a sugary soda,
or sometimes a lemonade.

00:03:59.159 --> 00:04:03.909
He often likes to tune into gaming streams
on Twitch, especially obscure indie titles,

00:04:03.909 --> 00:04:07.959
or, if he's feeling like something a bit more
familiar, Minecraft.

00:04:07.959 --> 00:04:11.579
But on this particular day, he has a visitor!

00:04:11.579 --> 00:04:16.430
SCP-507, the Reluctant Dimension Hopper, has
swung by with his own lunch to have a catch-up

00:04:16.430 --> 00:04:17.430
chat.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:21.410
A huge fan of meeting other friendly anomalies,
especially those completely different from

00:04:21.410 --> 00:04:26.900
himself, SCP-507 often stops by Cthulhu's
containment room whenever he happens to be

00:04:26.900 --> 00:04:28.470
in the same dimension.

00:04:28.470 --> 00:04:31.650
"Hey Squidward, how's it going?"

00:04:31.650 --> 00:04:36.759
SCP-2662 hasn't seen the show that this particular
nickname came from, but he enjoys being called

00:04:36.759 --> 00:04:40.620
a friendly name instead of some manner of
esoteric title.

00:04:40.620 --> 00:04:47.790
During this visit, SCP-507 shares stories
of his recent travels with SCP-2662, including

00:04:47.790 --> 00:04:52.070
his recent disturbing brush with the Smiling
Man, and his much more delightful time in

00:04:52.070 --> 00:04:56.470
a dimension where he found himself on a beach
where the sand was made of popcorn and the

00:04:56.470 --> 00:04:58.229
sea was made of Coca Cola.

00:04:58.229 --> 00:05:00.000
"Any weird cults come by lately?"

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.740
He asks, after finishing his story.

00:05:01.740 --> 00:05:05.220
"Not in a few weeks, tentacles crossed it
stays that way.

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:06.470
But you know my luck!

00:05:06.470 --> 00:05:10.660
Someone will probably be drawing arcane symbols
on the walls and doing weird chants in no

00:05:10.660 --> 00:05:11.660
time."

00:05:11.660 --> 00:05:13.910
"Bummer." 507 nodded sympathetically.

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.460
"Wanna play co-op for a bit?

00:05:15.460 --> 00:05:16.820
I haven't had time in forever."

00:05:16.820 --> 00:05:17.970
"Sure!"

00:05:17.970 --> 00:05:21.780
Even when it's a rare treat, it's always nice
to spend time with a friend doing something

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:23.400
you both love.

00:05:23.400 --> 00:05:29.050
Even if we can't relate to much about SCP-2662's
day-to-day life, we can at least relate to

00:05:29.050 --> 00:05:30.050
that.

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.199
It doesn't have to be gaming, either.

00:05:31.199 --> 00:05:35.810
It can be painting, baking, or even just watching
a tv show you love.

00:05:35.810 --> 00:05:40.120
The activity doesn't matter nearly as much
as the company, after all.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:41.590
1:30 PM.

00:05:41.590 --> 00:05:48.870
After about an hour of gaming with SCP-507,
SCP-2662 gets an unwelcome interruption.

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:52.970
Just when the two enter a new dungeon, ready
to take on the bosses waiting in there, right

00:05:52.970 --> 00:05:59.880
when SCP-2662 asks to be healed...SCP-507
disappears from his seat, popping over to

00:05:59.880 --> 00:06:04.320
wherever his anomalous dimension-hopping ability
dragged him to next.

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:05.569
"Oh...bye."

00:06:05.569 --> 00:06:10.430
He knows 507 can't hear him, but he wants
to bid him farewell just the same.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:14.470
He turns to his computer, and boots up a game
he can play by himself.

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:19.470
He only hopes his friend was sent somewhere
safe, and that he'll come back sometime soon.

00:06:19.470 --> 00:06:21.060
2:00 PM.

00:06:21.060 --> 00:06:26.000
At 2:00, SCP-2662 gets yet another unwelcome
interruption.

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:31.520
A loud boom rocks the room as explosives detonate
nearby, breaking a wall of the containment

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:32.710
unit open.

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:36.740
While the Mobile Task Force does their best
to subdue the invaders responsible, they are

00:06:36.740 --> 00:06:41.590
all knocked out by a grenade filled with an
unidentified form of sleeping gas.

00:06:41.590 --> 00:06:47.759
With no one to deter them, a group of strange
civilians in red robes come pouring into SCP-2662's

00:06:47.759 --> 00:06:48.940
room.

00:06:48.940 --> 00:06:55.060
"Oh great and powerful Lord of Darkness, we
come to free you from this infernal prison!"

00:06:55.060 --> 00:06:58.930
One man shouts, brandishing a candelabra filled
with lit black candles.

00:06:58.930 --> 00:07:00.740
"Oh, no thanks.

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:02.150
I'm good here."

00:07:02.150 --> 00:07:03.830
"But...we brought you an offering."

00:07:03.830 --> 00:07:08.509
Another man steps forward, tossing a bag of
dried bats onto 2662's bed.

00:07:08.509 --> 00:07:11.500
"Hey, oh man, I sleep there!

00:07:11.500 --> 00:07:12.500
Gross."

00:07:12.500 --> 00:07:13.500
Cthulhu groans.

00:07:13.500 --> 00:07:18.210
"We have thirteen more offerings, and then
the sacrificial ritual can commence!

00:07:18.210 --> 00:07:20.680
You just need to come with us so it can begin!

00:07:20.680 --> 00:07:25.850
The day of Great Freedom, when you will unleash
your thousand year reign of madness upon the

00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:26.850
land!"

00:07:26.850 --> 00:07:29.910
"I'm not really into madness, I'm more into
Overwatch."

00:07:29.910 --> 00:07:35.620
SCP-2662 backs away from the supplicants,
even as they come at him with more and more

00:07:35.620 --> 00:07:37.169
grotesque offerings.

00:07:37.169 --> 00:07:42.280
Cow tongues, unidentifiable mushrooms, one
woman tries to hand him a crying baby.

00:07:42.280 --> 00:07:45.500
He refuses each one, but they are persistent.

00:07:45.500 --> 00:07:49.530
As he is swatting away jars of pickled frogs,
a woman begins drawing a circle around the

00:07:49.530 --> 00:07:55.050
room in what he hopes is red paint, but fears
is something else entirely.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:57.639
"Um, thank you all for these gifts.

00:07:57.639 --> 00:08:00.570
You have proven yourself as loyal followers.

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:04.370
I'm going to stay here though, to, uh, spread
the madness.

00:08:04.370 --> 00:08:05.710
From here.

00:08:05.710 --> 00:08:06.979
You all can go on home."

00:08:06.979 --> 00:08:10.090
He tries to shoo them out, but they continue
to press closer.

00:08:10.090 --> 00:08:13.030
Thankfully, his rescue finally shows up.

00:08:13.030 --> 00:08:17.790
Task Force Tau-9 swoops in at this point and
begins knocking out and administering amnestics

00:08:17.790 --> 00:08:19.590
to all of the cultists.

00:08:19.590 --> 00:08:23.500
They may not be able to cure them of their
mad devotion, but they can at least make sure

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:27.120
the cult forgets the location of the containment
unit.

00:08:27.120 --> 00:08:29.289
At least, for a little while.

00:08:29.289 --> 00:08:33.750
They're able to dispense with these particular
intruders humanely, but they may need to use

00:08:33.750 --> 00:08:36.019
lethal force for the next ones.

00:08:36.019 --> 00:08:38.550
That's always a possibility.

00:08:38.550 --> 00:08:41.810
After the cultists have been removed from
the Site, some maintenance staff are called

00:08:41.810 --> 00:08:45.820
in to repair the damage to the wall where
the explosives knocked it in.

00:08:45.820 --> 00:08:51.140
While they work, SCP-2662 goes over his newspaper
one more time, making sure he didn't miss

00:08:51.140 --> 00:08:52.150
anything.

00:08:52.150 --> 00:08:56.660
Attention to detail is an important skill
to have, especially if one intends to get

00:08:56.660 --> 00:08:58.550
the most out of their everyday life.

00:08:58.550 --> 00:09:03.640
He finds a few editorials he neglected to
read before, and enjoys finishing up the newspaper

00:09:03.640 --> 00:09:04.800
in its entirety.

00:09:04.800 --> 00:09:06.269
4:00 PM.

00:09:06.269 --> 00:09:10.270
After the task force returns to their stations,
and the maintenance crew has finished fixing

00:09:10.270 --> 00:09:15.090
the wall, SCP-2662 turns to one of his newest
hobbies.

00:09:15.090 --> 00:09:18.940
He attempted to hide this pursuit from the
Foundation at first, but they agreed to let

00:09:18.940 --> 00:09:22.660
him try it out as long as he followed some
safety precautions.

00:09:22.660 --> 00:09:29.769
So now, at around 4 PM every day, SCP-2662
streams on his very own Twitch channel.

00:09:29.769 --> 00:09:34.570
He never uses identifying information, and
keeps his camera turned off the entire time

00:09:34.570 --> 00:09:39.000
lest the internet see his tentacled face,
but he does talk to the few viewers in his

00:09:39.000 --> 00:09:40.519
chat via a microphone.

00:09:40.519 --> 00:09:45.470
"What's up, it's SquidBoi2662, back to play
some games for you guys again.

00:09:45.470 --> 00:09:49.060
I hope you're all having a killer day, and
thanks for tuning in.

00:09:49.060 --> 00:09:51.930
Today I'm going to be checking out Apex Legends
for the very first time.

00:09:51.930 --> 00:09:55.070
A lot of you recommended this game to me,
so I'm stoked to check it out!"

00:09:55.070 --> 00:10:02.090
As his small fan community watches, SCP-2662
tries out the popular MMORPG, and plays his

00:10:02.090 --> 00:10:04.450
way through it for several hours.

00:10:04.450 --> 00:10:09.380
One person in the chat asks if he has ever
heard of "the great tentacled beast of legend,"

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:14.029
but he makes sure to block them before they
give the rest of the chat any ideas.

00:10:14.029 --> 00:10:18.240
He doesn't want people to watch his streams
because he's some famous elder god or something,

00:10:18.240 --> 00:10:20.890
he wants to be liked for who he is.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:22.060
7:00 PM.

00:10:22.060 --> 00:10:26.781
Every gamer needs to break for some fuel,
and SCP-2662 is no exception!

00:10:26.781 --> 00:10:31.970
At around 7, he wraps up his stream, thanks
all of his viewers and subscribers, and gets

00:10:31.970 --> 00:10:33.579
ready to have some dinner.

00:10:33.579 --> 00:10:39.050
He throws on another podcast, this time an
actual play podcast following a tabletop gaming

00:10:39.050 --> 00:10:42.070
campaign, and tucks into his last meal of
the day.

00:10:42.070 --> 00:10:45.820
Like all of his other meals, it varies from
day to day, but most of the time he goes with

00:10:45.820 --> 00:10:47.060
his favorite: pizza.

00:10:47.060 --> 00:10:52.210
A big cheese pizza, delivered from a local
pizza shop by a delivery boy who has received

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:57.079
more than his fair share of amnestics, and
can never remember why exactly this random

00:10:57.079 --> 00:10:59.840
unmarked building seems so familiar.

00:10:59.840 --> 00:11:04.080
Munching on his pizza and listening to tales
of magic and mayhem acted out by a group of

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:10.310
friends at a game table, SCP-2662 can't help
but feel just a little melancholy.

00:11:10.310 --> 00:11:14.450
He's happy with what he has, of course, but
he dreams of a normal life.

00:11:14.450 --> 00:11:18.959
The kind of life where he and his friends
could play games together or record a podcast.

00:11:18.959 --> 00:11:21.970
Where he could share this pizza with someone
else.

00:11:21.970 --> 00:11:25.800
But he might not ever have that, and it's
something he has to accept.

00:11:25.800 --> 00:11:30.890
He can still choose to appreciate what he
has, rather than mourn what he doesn't.

00:11:30.890 --> 00:11:34.930
After he's finished eating, and the episode
is finished, it's back to the grind at the

00:11:34.930 --> 00:11:35.930
computer.

00:11:35.930 --> 00:11:40.270
He turns on The Sims for a little while, constructing
the kind of normal life he likes to fantasize

00:11:40.270 --> 00:11:41.620
about sometimes.

00:11:41.620 --> 00:11:45.330
But then one of his Sims burns the house down
while trying to make eggs, and he gives up

00:11:45.330 --> 00:11:48.310
on that particular endeavor to play some Minecraft.

00:11:48.310 --> 00:11:49.930
11 PM.

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:55.070
Some nights the excitement keeps SCP-2662
awake and playing his games until the wee

00:11:55.070 --> 00:11:56.170
hours of the morning.

00:11:56.170 --> 00:12:01.459
Tonight, however, he finds himself exhausted
from an unexpectedly action-packed day, courtesy

00:12:01.459 --> 00:12:02.990
of those cultists.

00:12:02.990 --> 00:12:07.990
He powers down the game, turns on his final
podcast of the day, a guided meditation to

00:12:07.990 --> 00:12:11.190
wind him down for sleep, and climbs into bed.

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:15.459
Tomorrow, he'll get up and do it all again,
doing his best to carve out a little bit of

00:12:15.459 --> 00:12:18.350
peace in a strange, chaotic world.

00:12:18.350 --> 00:12:23.750
Maybe tomorrow he'll just be left alone, allowed
to be himself instead of what everyone expects

00:12:23.750 --> 00:12:24.750
him to be.

00:12:24.750 --> 00:12:27.130
He'll just have to stick it out and see.

00:12:27.130 --> 00:12:29.320
That's the beauty of this life, after all.

00:12:29.320 --> 00:12:31.320
Tomorrow is always a new day.

00:12:31.320 --> 00:12:33.850
Want to own an SCP of your own?

00:12:33.850 --> 00:12:37.529
Go to scpswag.com for premium anomalous merchandise!

00:12:37.529 --> 00:12:43.970
Now go check out “A Day in the Life of SCP-049”
and “What Does SCP-999 Do All Day?

00:12:43.970 --> 00:12:47.300
(Hour by Hour)” for more anomalous daily
routines!

